    "review_findings": [
      "Verified the fixed 46-file scope SHA and every on-disk SHA-256; all paths match. Canonical config and extension-draft configuration are identical, and the frozen agent trio is unchanged.",
      "The formal set covers seven own implementation pages, seven trait variants, and 15 real Mark bindings. The shared map and reverse weapon pages retain the same actual IDs, Mark names, restrictions, and trait item paths.",
      "I–IV values are .025/.05/.075/.10; the bilingual RAW keys and formatter reconstruction match, and available_tiers remains null.",
      "The controlled formula is B+F*(S+t): only the melee-critical finesse portion receives t, with weakspot and critical terms sharing S. The example states its no-forcefield/no-conversion and neutral-downstream assumptions. Hit Mass reduction and armor-abort behavior remain distinct; cumulative mass budget and breed abort remain.",
      "The corrected M1/M2/M3 shovel distinction is now singular and precise in SOURCE_INDEX and synchronized with the canonical/draft and formal variant text: M1 sweep punch; M2 no extra player movement; M3 special-active with pre-hit captured alive target can move the player backward, including if that hit then kills the target; no enemy push or extra damage Attack. The focused correction receipt matches the prior scope and is accepted.",
      "The 128px image receipt, game icon identifier/path, and attachment URL are separated and agree across canonical, map, and README. Existing applicable cache and special-route evidence was reused without broadening the claim."
    ],
    "verification": "Reviewed the fixed formal pages, RAW/reconstruction, tiers and formulas, variant and shared/reverse associations, corrected M3 delta, and verified all scoped file hashes. No remaining substantive issue was found."
